VeridianOS: KWin: ecm_setup_qtplugin_macro_names with MACRO_NAMES

ECM warned (ECMSetupQtPluginMacroNames.cmake:131): "For ECM >= 6.18, use
the MACRO_NAMES argument instead of the JSON_* ones". The four effect
factory macros are now given as MACRO_NAMES, as upstream KWin master
does; with ECM 6.18 and later the JSON_ARGn positions are no longer used
(moc's own dependency output tracks the JSON files), so AutoMoc behaves
the same.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -475,12 +475,10 @@
 )
 
 ecm_setup_qtplugin_macro_names(
-    JSON_ARG2
+    MACRO_NAMES
         "KWIN_EFFECT_FACTORY"
-    JSON_ARG3
         "KWIN_EFFECT_FACTORY_ENABLED"
         "KWIN_EFFECT_FACTORY_SUPPORTED"
-    JSON_ARG4
         "KWIN_EFFECT_FACTORY_SUPPORTED_ENABLED"
     CONFIG_CODE_VARIABLE
         PACKAGE_SETUP_KWINEFFECTS_AUTOMOC_VARIABLES
